course: dictionary
lesson: 15501
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, their context, tell you which meaning the writer means. «The pigs went back into their sty before dark.» Here a sty is a pen or small building where pigs are kept.
explain: «My bedroom is a sty after the party!» Here sty does not mean a pig pen. It is an informal way of saying a room is very dirty or messy. Always ask: does this meaning fit the sentence?
explain: «A sty on my eyelid made it red and sore.» Here the word is spelled stye, and it means a small, sore lump on the edge of the eye. Sty and stye are said the same way, so the context is what tells you which one you are reading.
fact: A sty is a pen or small building where pigs are kept.
fact: Informally, a sty can mean a very dirty or messy place, like a messy bedroom.
fact: A stye (also spelled sty) is a small, red, sore lump on the edge of the eyelid, caused by an infection.
fact: A stye is usually harmless, but do not squeeze it. A warm cloth and clean hands can help.
exercise: «The pigs rolled in the mud in their sty.» Where do the pigs live? | A bath | *A pen where pigs are kept | A busy shop | A field of wheat
exercise: «After the party, my bedroom was a total sty.» What does sty mean here? | A lump on the eyelid | A small pig | *A very messy place | A quiet garden
exercise: «I have a stye in my eye, so it is red and sore.» What is a stye? | A kind of cloth | *A small, red, sore lump on the eyelid | A pig pen | A type of bird
test: «The farmer cleaned out the sty.» Which meaning fits? | A bedroom | A bee's home | *A pen for pigs | An eye
test: Dad says, «Use a warm cloth on the stye, and do not squeeze it.» What should you do? | Squeeze it hard | Rub it with dirty hands | Cover it with mud | *Put a warm cloth on it
exam: «The stye on his eyelid was not serious, but it looked sore.» What is a stye? | A messy room | A type of insect | *A small, sore lump on the eyelid | A pig pen
